   {
    "text": "**A Longlasting War**\n\nIn shadowed halls where iron clanged,  \nA battle raged with no end in sight.  \nThe skies were torn by thunder's cry,  \nAnd voices rose in desperate fight.  \n\nThe land was scarred, the people torn,  \nBy greed and strife, by hatred born.  \nThe years passed slow, the years grew deep,  \nA war that lasted, and never slept.  \n\nThe soldiers marched, their hearts were worn,  \nTheir dreams were shattered, their hopes were gone.  \nThe world was changed, the peace was lost,  \nA war that never truly was at rest.  \n\nYet in the end, the truth was clear—  \nThe war was long, but not the war we knew.  \nFor in the end, the peace was won,  \nBy those who chose to see the light.  \n\n---\n\n**P.P.S.**  \nA long-lasting war is not just in time,  \nBut in the hearts of those who fight and live.  \nIt's in the scars that remain, the cost of peace,  \nAnd the hope that grows from the ashes of war.",
